    <dataSetInformation>
      <common:UUID>c1b5928c-fb2c-4c6f-988c-2381823b7f2d</common:UUID>
      <name>
        <baseName xml:lang="en">Pizza sauce, processing, at plant in Northern Italy, 1 kg Pizza sauce</baseName>
      </name>
      <common:synonyms>1 kg di Salsa Pizza, trasformazione allo stabilimento, Nord Italia</common:synonyms>
      <classificationInformation>
        <common:classification name="ILCDCategories" classes="../ILCDClassification.xml">
          <common:class level="0">Materials production</common:class>
          <common:class level="1">Food and renewable raw materials</common:class>
        </common:classification>
      </classificationInformation>
      <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">The dataset has been developed within the Arcadia Project. It concerns the processing of industrial tomatoes in reference to the report “Studio LCA della filiera dell’industria del pomodoro confezionato in Italia”.</common:generalComment>
    </dataSetInformation>
    <quantitativeReference type="Reference flow(s)">
      <referenceToReferenceFlow>0</referenceToReferenceFlow>
    </quantitativeReference>
    <time>
      <common:referenceYear>2021</common:referenceYear>
      <common:dataSetValidUntil>2028</common:dataSetValidUntil>
    </time>
    <geography>
      <locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction location="IT">
        <descriptionOfRestrictions>Italy. Primary data collected in the North Italy. Representative dataset of North Italian tomato chain production.</descriptionOfRestrictions>
      </locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction>
    </geography>
    <technology>
      <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>Tomato puree, made from tomatoes grown in the field, transported to the producing company. The production process begins with a quick boiling of the tomatoes to facilitate the removal of the skins. The tomatoes are then separated from skins and seeds through refining machines. The extracted juices are then heated in a special machine that promotes the evaporation of the water to achieve the correct density of the puree. The finished product is thus packaged.  Pizza sauce is prepared with only the best Italian tomatoes and a pinch of oregano, onion and basil. Primary (North Italian supply chain) and secondary (literature and/or industry data) data representative of the North Italian supply chain in terms of geographic characteristics and technologies used (machinery, equipment, etc.) were collected. Inventory data were collected as physical quantities of materials used in different processes. The benefits from the use of secondary materials produced by recycling waste materials (e.g., plastics and cardboard) were excluded.&#13;
Background data were modelled according to Ecoinvent v. 3.8</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
      <technologicalApplicability>Salsa Aromatica per Pizza is made with only the best Italian tomatoes and a pinch of oregano, onion and basil. With its slightly coarse texture, this sauce goes very well with homemade pizza, to which it gives the full flavors of tomatoes with a slight spiciness.</technologicalApplicability>
    </technology>
  </processInformation>
